# Commits that moved or reformatted code without changing behaviour.
#
# `git blame` follows the last commit to touch a line, so a formatting sweep or
# a file split re-points every line in it at that sweep, and the change that
# actually introduced the line stops being reachable from it. Decomposition work
# moves a lot of lines, so those commits are listed here rather than allowed to
# bury the history.
#
# Enable it once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# Only add a commit that provably changed no behaviour -- a pure move, a
# re-export split, a formatter run. If in doubt, leave it out: a wrongly-listed
# commit hides the change that actually caused a bug.
